{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["כי לא לו יהיה הזרע — and they were particular about this." "נתן זרע — hatef qamatz. For every word whose accent (te'am) is on the final letter and has a malefowam (=qamatz), and the word joined (samukh) to it whose accent is on the first letter — they are in maqqef and the malefowam turns into hatef qamatz. And likewise: ארך אפים וגדל חסד. And: ואם שלש אלה לא יעשה לה. But: את שלש הערים — malefowam it is."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {1 "Rashbam's technical phonological discussion uses malefowam as his term for the vowel qamatz (a long o-type vowel in his tradition), and explains that under maqqef with a word whose accent falls on the first letter, it reduces to hatef qamatz. The three biblical examples illustrate the rule (first two) and the exception (third, no maqqef)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:39.001257625Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}